##DESCRIPTION
##  Contour plot basics problem, MAT237 A2 worksheet 5.1-5.2
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('multivariable calculus', 'contour plot', 'real-valued functions’)

## DBsubject('Multivariable Calculus')
## DBchapter('Fundamentals')
## DBsection('Real-valued functions')
## Date('9/7/2023')
## Author('')
## Institution('University of Toronto')
## TitleText1('MAT237 Worksheets')
## EditionText1('')
## AuthorText1('')
## Section1('A2')
## Problem1('5.1-5.2')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");

$dd = DropDown([ "A", "B", "C", "D", "E" ], "E");

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_PGML
A topographic map of the island of Hawaii is below. The contour plot values are measured in feet.

>>[!A map of Hawaii with contour lines.!]{'a2-hawaii.png'}{250}<<

Let [`h: \mathbb{R}^2\to\mathbb{R}`] be a function describing the height of the island at a point.

a) On which level set of [`h`] does the point [`A`] belong? [_]{Real(1000)}

b) Among the points [`A,B,C,D,E`], which point is the 3rd highest? [_]{$dd}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) 1000

b) The correct answer is [$dd].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
